{"id": "DfOr9i3xkrb", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Why did Parshurama fight the king with 1000 arms? This king once caught RAVANA like a monkey. Then he stole a cow from Parshurama's father. Big mistake. 🪓\n\nKing Kartavirya Arjuna of the Haihayas worshipped Lord Dattatreya and was blessed with 1000 arms.\n\nPlaying in the Narmada with his queens, he stopped the river with his arms. The water flowed back and flooded Ravana's camp. Ravana picked a fight, and the king caught him \"like a monkey\", locked him up in Mahishmati, and let him go.\n\nOne day, out hunting, the king came to the ashram of Sage Jamadagni. The sage fed the king and his whole army from his wish-cow, Kamadhenu. A sage richer than a king? The king wanted her. His men dragged her away, crying, with her calf.\n\nRama came home. The cow was gone. He took up his axe, his bow, his shield and his quiver, and went after the king.\n\nThe king sent 17 armies (akshauhinis). Rama fought them alone. The king shot arrows from 500 bows at once. Rama cut them all down with one bow. The king tore up hills and trees to throw. One axe. 1000 arms.\n\nRama brought the cow home, with her calf. But his father was not proud. \"We are brahmins, son. We are honoured for our forgiveness.\" So Rama went on a pilgrimage for a whole year to atone. 🙏\n\n📖 Source: Bhagavata Purana 9.15.17–41 and 9.16.1. The Mahabharata (Vana Parva 3.116) tells it too, more briefly (there Rama cuts the 1000 arms with arrows); Ravana's capture is also in the Valmiki Ramayana (Uttara Kanda).\n\nThis is Part 4 of our Parshurama series. Every part stands on its own, so start anywhere!\n\n📚 The Navadurga Set, kids' picture books on the nine forms of Maa Durga, is out now at rishikatha.com (link in bio).\n\n💬 Ravana lost to Kartavirya. Kartavirya lost to Parshurama. WHO HUMBLED PARSHURAMA? Tell us in the comments 👇\n🔁 Share it with someone who thinks they know every Ravana story.\n📌 Save it for later.\n\n#parshurama #parashurama #kartavirya #sahasrarjuna #ravana #kamadhenu #jamadagni #dattatreya #vishnuavatar #dashavatar #bhagavatapurana #hindumythology #sanatandharma #rishikatha #jaiparshuram", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1793601783, "like_count": 6697, "comment_count": 56, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1876686130177456a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 51.742, "asr": 48000, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr2-2.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQMkdIT-tGTvfQ240kqf6aPmFx131NL7aw65SGYZzuyEdNNWFVWdIt9GypqtRO9kIKXKU0MQPSl9hH2-d438KCRpT-7y5ND-RFpHrYY.mp4?_nc_cat=109&_nc_oc=AdrSxostlXGISC2yo8Lmvq8bzLvYhfR227JIkJmONaQJfSufb87G26je08y_4BkuLlv7Jno2rE4zKNSDPfV2rPEI&_nc_sid=9ca052&_nc_ht=instagram.fblr2-2.fna.fbcdn.net&_nc_ohc=TWjQdlvKc2gQ7kNvwFw7mot&&ccb=17-1&_nc_gid=9GC3RfVDb5dm3pgAZGfU7g&_nc_ss=70689&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&_nc_zt=28&oh=00_AQRqTslwQu-e_iumRuruq1lt5FBbSGwilUAdx9tLsH5HVA&oe=6AF4208A", "manifest_stream_number": 0, "is_dash_periods": true, "protocol": "https", "audio_ext": "m4a", "video_ext": "none", "vbr": 0, "abr": 51.742, "resolution": "audio only", "http_headers": {"User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/145.0.0.0 Safari/537.36", "Accept": "text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,*/*;q=0.8", "Accept-Language": "en-us,en;q=0.5", "Sec-Fetch-Mode": "navigate", "Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "format": "dash-1876686130177456a - audio only (DASH audio)"}, {"url": "https://instagram.fblr2-2.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m86/AQOT6nNpgX3K5nz8HGSGN6BCmZPA5ZyPjIwIiQV6IHXp3Z5-aK1ftKlOlQhrGJIZ8TD0OjGRRouLT8DrqAkUGW3WdqTomJn1QA7pwYM.mp4?_nc_cat=107&_nc_oc=AdrFQVKU1u7ZPs97YuKQH0xlOlztYMDsbpe4dwa9-rqbFGI_mrOgJHZ3BkrAWNw2nVcQns7WcP7LhU213rjb22ZA&_nc_sid=5e9851&_nc_ht=instagram.fblr2-2.fna.fbcdn.net&_nc_ohc=YLf